From 9127b260a9f46ebfbcd56acf19c546fd707e5318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:35:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: optionally stream recorded commands to the host
 before submit

With VulkanQueueSubmitWithCommands a command buffer is staged in the guest
and sent at submit, so the host decodes it only after the guest finished
recording, and the next synchronous call waits behind the whole decode.
debug.velox.cmd_stream_kb=N sends the staged commands with
vkQueueFlushCommandsGOOGLE at a command boundary once N KiB are staged; the
host appends them to the same host command buffer and the rest goes at
submit. Skipped for secondary command buffers, after vkCmdExecuteCommands
and with auxiliary command memory. Descriptor sets bound so far are
committed first, as at submit. The staging stream is flushed before
reading its size: commands encoded since the last commit sit in the
IOStream allocation and reset() would drop them (a first version lost them;
caught by dEQP-VK.api.command_buffers.record_many_draws_primary_2).

vk-render draws (20000 draws/frame) on WHPX + ASG: 786 -> 1028 frames/s
with 256 KiB; game/sync unchanged; image checksums identical. dEQP with
16 KiB: api.command_buffers, binding_model.descriptor_update,
synchronization.basic, draw.renderpass basic/indexed, push_constant pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

